AWS services are listed below.
Service	What you should understand
EC2	Compute, AMIs, instance types, EBS, security groups, user data, Auto Scaling
S3	Buckets, objects, IAM, versioning, lifecycle, encryption, replication, static hosting
RDS	MySQL/PostgreSQL, Multi-AZ, backups, snapshots, read replicas
DynamoDB	NoSQL, partition keys, sort keys, indexes, capacity modes
VPC	Subnets, route tables, IGW, NAT Gateway, NACL, Security Groups
IAM	Users, groups, roles, policies, STS, least privilege
Lambda	Serverless functions, triggers, permissions, layers, concurrency
API Gateway	REST/HTTP APIs, authentication, throttling, integrations
CloudFront	CDN, caching, origins, distributions, invalidation
SQS	Queues, producers/consumers, visibility timeout, DLQ
SNS	Pub/sub, notifications, fan-out
CloudWatch	Metrics, logs, alarms, dashboards, log insights
CloudTrail	AWS API auditing and security investigation
CloudFormation	Infrastructure as Code
EKS	Managed Kubernetes on AWS
Step Functions	Orchestrating multi-step workflows
